course: dictionary
lesson: 13474
title: Hyperlinks: click to go
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hyperlink is a word, picture or button that takes you somewhere else when you click it. It can take you to another web page, a website or a file. «Click the hyperlink to watch the video» means press the link to go to the video.
explain: Hyperlink can also be a verb. To hyperlink something means to turn it into a link. «Ravi will hyperlink his project to the map» means Ravi will make his project into a link that opens the map.
explain: Hyperlinks join web pages together, and that is how the World Wide Web is built. But a link can also be a trap. Before you click, look at where it will take you, especially if it came in an email or a message.
fact: A hyperlink is a word, picture or button that you click to go to another page, website or file.
fact: «Click the hyperlink» means press the link to go to the new place.
fact: Hyperlinks join web pages together to make the World Wide Web.
fact: Some hyperlinks in emails or messages lead to scams, so check a link before you click it.
fact: «Insert a hyperlink» means add a link into your document or slide.
exercise: «Click the hyperlink to see the picture of the volcano.» What is a hyperlink? | A type of hard drive | A password you type to log in | A cable that connects your computer to the printer | *A word, picture or button you click to go somewhere else
exercise: Ravi says, «I will hyperlink my project to the map.» What does hyperlink mean here? | To draw a map by hand | To print the map | *To make the project into a link to the map | To delete the project
exercise: An email says, «Click here to claim your prize!» Before you click, what should you do? | *Check where the link leads first | Click quickly before the link disappears | Forward it to all your friends | Type your password on the page
test: Which of these can be a hyperlink? | A ruler | A pencil case | *A picture on a web page that opens another page | A paper bus timetable
test: Why should you check a link before clicking it? | It makes the link louder | Links are too small to see | Links always lead to the same page | *Some links lead to scams
exam: Which sentence uses hyperlink as a verb? | The hyperlink is a blue button on the top of the page | *Please hyperlink the photo to your report | Click the hyperlink to open the file | A hyperlink is on the screen
